-- NORM-LOG N10 goal A: a continuation's guard reads the ledger of the party whose hand-off armed it,
-- also when the continuation is resumed event by event inside a compound (skeptic-design S1).
-- Pass: all three traces FULFILLED (the borrow is allowed), as before A.
IMPORT prelude
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF patron, clerk
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF giveBack, borrow, stamp
GIVETH DEONTIC Person Action
c MEANS
  PARTY patron MUST giveBack WITHIN 14
  HENCE RECORD `returned` IS TRUE
  HENCE (PARTY patron MAY borrow PROVIDED RECALL `returned` EQUALS JUST TRUE WITHIN 100)
GIVETH DEONTIC Person Action
other MEANS PARTY clerk MAY stamp WITHIN 100
-- bare RECALL in the continuation's guard reads the ledger of the party whose
-- hand-off is still in scope (patron), because today the continuation scans
-- the rest of the stream inside that scope
#TRACE c AT 0 WITH PARTY patron DOES giveBack AT 1   PARTY patron DOES borrow AT 2
#TRACE c RAND other AT 0 WITH PARTY patron DOES giveBack AT 1   PARTY patron DOES borrow AT 2
#TRACE other RAND c AT 0 WITH PARTY patron DOES giveBack AT 1   PARTY patron DOES borrow AT 2
